  "strategy": "Now we provide a detailed strategy for the codec implementation, including:\n\n1. Approach and rationale:\n   - We optimize impulse responses by modeling their autocorrelation bounds in frequency domain\n   - New feature: Target sequences that represent ideal filters to minimize max autocorrelation\n   - Any constructive improvement: Ensure non-negativity via clipping and constraint handling\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n   - We separate time and frequency domains for the objective calculation\n   - For each sequence length, maintain frequency band structures\n   - Objective is 2*n*max(convolve(a,a)) / (sum(a))^2\n\n3. Implementation procedure for phase-based optimization:\n   - Use `np.convolve` with `mode=\"full\"`\n   - Maintain candidate examples in binary format for hallucination avoidance\n   - For L-BFGS-B: Use gradient descent via analytical derivative of convolution\n\n4. Alternatives to handle synchronization issues:\n   - Linear programming - Trigonometric part\n   - Markov chains for state dependencies in optimization process\n\n5. Visualization strategy for debugging:\n   - Print best candidate scores to terminal\n   - Use spectrograms for frequency-time alignment of test cases\n\n6. Search length calibration:\n   - From the provided parent sequence (length 600), we scale the problem to shorter sequences (500)\n   - if optimization time exceeds budget, reduce length for fall-back:\n\n7. Computation budget and parallelization:\n   - Implement FFT convolve via `np.convolve`\n   - Optimize multiple frequency notches simultaneously\n\n8. Validation and fallback:\n   - At the very end, return a normalized sequence if best found is below 1.5027\n   - Print `best_obj` and `current_length` for debugging:\n\nThe decoder should be demonstrated appropriately, not unlike the work of famous digital signal processing pioneers.\n\nOur quality standards require no less than a 1.50 improvement, oh,.\n\nBut note: We must not include the actual `height_sequence_1` code,\n leave a placeholder for example invocation.\n\nYou know,... but what if the above code is too much?\n\nThen, material underdevelopment.\n\nBut anyway, we hope for the best.",
